      "excerpt": "Knowledge base for the naval fire safety training simulator built in Unreal Engine 5.8.",
      "body": "# ⚓ NavalFireVR — Vault Home\n\nKnowledge base for the naval fire safety training simulator built in Unreal Engine 5.8.\nOpen this folder in Obsidian as a vault.\n\n> One-line goal: detailed naval fire safety simulation where a trainee picks a **role** and a **fire scenario** from a main menu, then plays a shipboard exercise.\n\n## Core notes\n\n- [[Project Overview]] — what the project is, key paths, current status\n- [[Project Dashboard — Status]] — recorded state on the project website; the vault syncs to the site\n- [[Curriculum & Sources]] — the four French naval safety lectures, slide traceability\n- [[Roles & Command Chain]] — playable roles and the organic command structure\n- [[Objective Guide]] — French in-game instruction line, RDR2 style\n- [[Menu System]] — main menu, 42 routes, controls, builder\n- [[All 42 Worlds]] — every role × fire route, level path, and current content\n- [[Ship Environments]] — expanded ship, reference corridor, bow & sea scenery\n- [[Fire Drill Scenario]] — the kitchen electrical-fire CO2 drill (first playable slice)\n- [[Signage]] — the installed readable signage system\n- [[Input & Controller]] — mouse capture, desktop + VR input\n- [[2026-11-05 — Gameplay Updates]] — latest saved guide, French sign, reset, and desktop controls\n\n## Reference indexes\n\n- [[Python Scripts Index]] — every tool script in `Tools\\Python` and how to run it\n- [[Docs Index]] — every guide in `Tools\\Docs`\n- [[Decision Log]] — chronological record of decisions and updates\n- [[Objective Guide]] — installed French in-game guide · [[TODO — Roadmap]] — open work: Classe F conversion, role objectives, profiling\n- [[Project Preferences]] — user rules mirrored from `AGENTS.md`\n\n## Quick facts\n\n| Item | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Unreal project | `C:\\Users\\user\\Documents\\Unreal Projects\\NavalFireVR` |\n| Startup / game map | `/Game/NavalFireVR/Menu_v1/L_NavalMenu` |\n| Default drill map | `/Game/NavalFireVR/ExpandedShip/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Expanded` |\n| Menu default selection | groupe d'attaque × Classe F |\n| Route manifest | `Tools\\Docs\\MENU_ROUTES.json` |\n| Main reference doc | `Tools\\Docs\\NAVAL_SIMULATION_REFERENCE.md` |\n| Engine | Unreal 5.8.4 (forward rendering, Python Editor Script Plugin) |\n\n⚠️ Note: rendering/API behavior notes here were recorded 2026-11-02/03. Re-verify against the live project before big changes.\n\n## Latest ship graphics update — 2026-11-07\n\n- [[Ship Realism — Imported Environment]] — applied wall panels, detailed hatch hardware, equipment surface finishes, all ten compartments, both ship maps, previews and recovery records.\n- [[2026-11-07]] — daily record; saved-map checks passed, headset performance remains untested.\n",
