      "body": "# Docs Index\n\nEverything in the Unreal project's `Tools\\Docs` folder (`C:\\Users\\user\\Documents\\Unreal Projects\\NavalFireVR\\Tools\\Docs`).\n\n## Guides\n\n| File | What it covers | Vault note |\n|---|---|---|\n| `RUN_SECUREX.md` | Original corridor generator: usage, build contents, desktop preview, lighting repair | [[Ship Environments]] |\n| `RUN_EXPANDED_SHIP.md` | Expanded ship builder: layout tables, kitchen, validation scope | [[Ship Environments]] |\n| `RUN_BOW_SEA.md` | Bow + animated sea add-on: contents, animation, perf limits | [[Ship Environments]] |\n| `RUN_FIRE_DRILL.md` | Kitchen CO2 drill: install, controls, VR bindings, validation history | [[Fire Drill Scenario]] |\n| `RUN_FIRE_LOCKERS.md` | Four fire-equipment wardrobes, 21 equipment items, labels and recovery notes | [[Fire Equipment Lockers — MCP Repair & Readability]] |\n| `RUN_NAVAL_MENU.md` | Menu: controls, 42 routes, builder rules, verification | [[Menu System]] |\n| `RUN_EXPERIENCE_FIXES.md` | Sea v2, door rotation fix, mouse capture, menu input verification | [[Input & Controller]] |\n| `RUN_NAVAL_GUIDE.md` | French objective guide (RDR2 style): install, messages, rebinding rules | [[Objective Guide]] |\n| `RUN_NAVAL_SIGN_AND_RESTART.md` | French galley isolation sign and Backspace return to start | [[Signage]], [[Fire Drill Scenario]] |\n| `RUN_NAVAL_AZERTY_CONTROLS.md` | ZQSD movement, Ctrl crouch, Shift sprint | [[Input & Controller]] |\n| `STARTUP_MAP.md` | Startup map settings, editor camera, opening NavalFireVR | [[Project Overview]] |\n| `READABLE_SIGNAGE.md` | Signage style, coverage, repair script | [[Signage]] |\n\n## Reference / data files\n\n| File | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| `NAVAL_SIMULATION_REFERENCE.md` | **Master reference** — goal, curriculum, roles, structure, dated status updates. Read at the start of any NavalFireVR work |\n| `MCP_FIRE_LOCKERS_REPAIR.json` | Actual wardrobe actor references, backup map and saved MCP repair evidence |\n| `MENU_ROUTES.json` | Complete manifest of all 42 role × fire-type routes |\n| `NAVAL_SAFETY_SOURCE.json` | Slide-indexed text of the 4 French lecture decks (115 slides) — design must cite deck + slide |\n| `MENU_ART_PROMPT.md` | Record of the menu artwork generation prompt |\n| `EXPERIENCE_V2_REPORT.json` | Report data from the experience polish pass |\n| `SIGNAGE_REPORT.json` | Report data from the signage pass |\n| `NavalSafetySources\\` | Copies of the original `.ppt` decks + 8 JPEG photos (visual details live only here, not in text extraction) |\n| Previews | `MENU_PREVIEW.png`, `SEA_PREVIEW_v2.png`, `DOOR_PREVIEW_v2.png`, `SIGNAGE_PREVIEW.png` |\n\n## External source\n\n- Original lecture folder: `C:\\Users\\user\\Desktop\\AJ\\3eme-moi\\SOE\\Sécurité navale` → see [[Curriculum & Sources]]\n\n## Related\n\n[[Python Scripts Index]] · [[Project Preferences]] · [[Fire Equipment Lockers — MCP Repair & Readability]]\n\n## Ship realism records — 2026-11-07\n\n[[Ship Realism — Imported Environment]] links vault copies of the whole-ship guide, initial corridor guide, placement/material manifests, hardware/polish/orientation/surface-finish records, saved-map verification and acceptance ledger. Project originals use the `SHIP_ENVIRONMENT_` and `SHIP_REALISM_` prefixes in `Tools\\Docs`; eleven final previews are in `Tools\\Docs\\ShipRealismPreviews`. Vault previews/records are under `_attachments/ShipRealism`.\n",
