      "excerpt": "All scripts live in the Unreal project at C:\\Users\\user\\Documents\\Unreal Projects\\NavalFireVR\\Tools\\Python.",
      "body": "# Python Scripts Index\n\nAll scripts live in the Unreal project at `C:\\Users\\user\\Documents\\Unreal Projects\\NavalFireVR\\Tools\\Python`.\n**How to run:** open the `.uproject`, open the target map, **stop Play**, then in **Output Log → Cmd** paste:\n`py \"C:/Users/user/Documents/Unreal Projects/NavalFireVR/Tools/Python/<script>.py\"`\n(Alternative: File → Execute Python Script.) Requires the **Python Editor Script Plugin** (+ Editor Scripting Utilities). Results are saved Blueprints/assets — no runtime Python.\n\nHelper modules must stay **beside** the script that imports them (same folder).\n\n## Environment & ship builders\n\n| Script | Purpose | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `build_securex_environment.py` | Original SECUREX reference corridor generator → `/Game/NavalFireVR/ReferenceEnvironment/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Coursive` | Rerun = new numbered build; writes source texture under `Saved/SECUREX_Generated`; **contains shared geometry helpers imported by everything else — keep it beside every builder** |\n| `build_securex_expanded.py` | Expanded ship → `/Game/NavalFireVR/ExpandedShip/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Expanded` | 48 m ship, 10 rooms, kitchen; imports environment helpers; rerun = new Build_00N |\n| `build_naval_menu.py` | Menu builder (`L_NavalMenu`) | **Refuses to replace existing menu assets** — use a new version folder for revisions; needs `securex_blueprints.py` beside it |\n| `add_securex_bow_sea.py` | Adds bow + animated sea to the currently open expanded map | Idempotent; preserves interior/GameMode; needs `build_securex_environment.py` beside it |\n| `build_securex_expanded.py` / lighting | Uses repaired unshadowed point-light approach — no lighting repair needed for new builds | see [[Ship Environments]] |\n\n## Drill & gameplay\n\n| Script | Purpose | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `add_securex_fire_drill.py` | Adds kitchen CO2 drill to the open expanded map | Idempotent; helpers: `securex_blueprints.py`, `securex_fire_logic.py`, `securex_vr_logic.py`, `securex_fire_audio.py`, `build_securex_environment.py` |\n| `upgrade_securex_bottles.py` | Repairs bottle input keys, converts 7 old scenery extinguishers to usable CO2 cylinders | Needs `securex_bottle_logic.py`; preserves existing 8th cylinder; current drill uses Backspace reset |\n| `securex_fire_logic.py` | Flame pockets, suppression, re-ignition logic helper | Import helper, not run directly |\n| `securex_fire_audio.py` | Generated positional audio helper | Import helper |\n| `securex_vr_logic.py` | XRFramework VR bindings helper | Import helper |\n| `securex_bottle_logic.py` | Per-bottle charge/pin/grab state helper | Import helper |\n| `securex_blueprints.py` | Shared Blueprint-building helpers | Imported by menu + drill builders |\n\n## Navigation & desktop mode\n\n| Script | Purpose | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `enable_securex_desktop.py` | Creates map-specific desktop GameMode + inspection pawn; adds Z/Q mappings for DefaultPawn | Not a full walking Character; ZQSD + mouse |\n| `install_naval_azerty_controls.py` | Installs a new saved desktop pawn and selects it in the desktop GameMode | ZQSD replaces WASD; hold Ctrl crouch; hold Shift sprint; see [[Input & Controller]] |\n| `fix_securex_startup_view.py` | Restores/verifies kitchen editor camera view; enables Game View | Press G in editor viewport to show helper icons again |\n\n## Updates & polish (2026-11-02 generation)\n\n| Script | Purpose | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `polish_naval_experience.py` | Sea v2 appearance, door-frame rotation fix, gameplay mouse capture, menu input fixes | Needs `build_naval_menu.py` + `securex_blueprints.py` beside it; updates existing versioned assets **in place** and marks corrected geometry so reruns don't rotate again |\n| `improve_naval_signage.py` | Installs readable signage style on all TextRender labels | Marks corrected orientations; reruns reuse backing panels; assets `/Game/NavalFireVR/Signage_v1` |\n| `repair_securex_commands.py` | Repairs generator command sequence / classes | Earlier fix pass |\n| `repair_securex_lighting.py` | Repairs old builds' shadowed lights → unshadowed point lights + exposure | Idempotent; targets generator-tagged lights and `Neutral_Interior_Exposure` only; brightness knobs: `EXPOSURE_COMPENSATION`, `LIGHT_LUMENS`, `SHADOWS` near top of generator file |\n| `add_naval_guide.py` | Installs the French RDR2-style objective guide HUD on the drill map | Current v6: enlarged white/yellow text, Backspace reset; `GuideState()` created once per drill; every run makes a new HUD revision; selects the playable `FireDrill\\Controls_00N` class; see `RUN_NAVAL_GUIDE.md` |\n| `fix_naval_sign_and_restart.py` | Saves the galley sign as « Alimentation électrique » and corrects Backspace return to standing start height | Corrected run succeeded 2026-11-05; see [[Signage]] and [[Fire Drill Scenario]] |\n\n⚠️ **Rotation-order pitfall:** always use explicit pitch/yaw/roll keywords in geometry builders — positional rotation arguments once produced sideways door frames (see [[Ship Environments]]).\n\n## Related\n\n[[Docs Index]] · [[Project Preferences]]\n\n## Ship realism scripts — applied 2026-11-07\n\nAll project copies remain together in `C:\\Users\\user\\Documents\\Unreal Projects\\NavalFireVR\\Tools\\Python`.\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `ship_realism_inventory.py` | Read-only inspection inventory |\n| `ship_realism_whole_ship.py` | Main wall, service-fitting and copied-material installation |\n| `ship_realism_hardware.py` | Detailed parked hatch leaves and machine exhausts |\n| `ship_realism_polish.py` | Generic normal correction and wall kickplates |\n| `ship_realism_panel_orientation.py` | Correct detailed panel faces |\n| `ship_realism_surface_noise.py` | Generate/import final neutral roughness grain |\n| `ship_realism_verify.py` | Reload saved maps and verify assignments, collision, room coverage, signs and GameMode |\n| `ship_realism_finalize.py` | Panel orientation followed by saved-map verification |\n\nThese installers have already been executed. Do not blindly rerun them on upgraded maps; use the verification command in [[Ship Realism — Imported Environment]]. The pack does not supply complete replacement equipment models.\n",
