      "excerpt": "Known pitfall: older builders passed rotation as positional args, which Unreal read as roll/pitch/yaw → door frames/bow rails protruded sideways. Fixed by explicit pitch/yaw/rol…",
      "body": "# Ship Environments\n\n## 1. Expanded SECUREX ship — the drill map\n\n- Map: `/Game/NavalFireVR/ExpandedShip/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Expanded`\n- Builder: `Tools\\Python\\build_securex_expanded.py` (+ `build_securex_environment.py` helpers). Reruns create another numbered `Build_00N`; the old corridor map and its edits are preserved\n- Interior deck: 48 m long, ~15 m wide, 3 m central corridor, 3 m ceiling. X increases toward the bow; PlayerStart near the stern\n\n| Stern → Bow | Port side | Starboard side |\n|---|---|---|\n| Aft | Technical stores | Firefighting equipment room |\n| Middle-aft | Machinery room | Machine control room |\n| Midship | Workshop | Security briefing room |\n| Forward | Crew mess | Kitchen |\n| Furthest forward | Forward stores | Pantry / forward stores |\n\n- Ten rooms, open entrances from the corridor; port-side internal hatches form a second route; kitchen is 24 m forward of the control-room entrance, with a storage compartment beyond\n- **Kitchen**: approximation of a supplied photo — stainless counters, double sink, cooker/oven, extraction hoods, central prep table, open kettles, extinguisher + fire-blanket cabinet. `SECUREX_FIRE_ORIGIN_GALLEY` target point (tag `SECUREX_FireOrigin`) above the cooker — placement anchor for fire systems, no flames itself\n- **Firefighting store**: decorative racks (hoses, BA cylinders, suits, helmets, axes, first-aid, stretcher). Visual assortment only — **no pickup or firefighting behavior yet**\n- Outliner groups: Galley, Firefighting_Store, Control_Room, Machinery, Workshop_And_Mess… Camera actors `Kitchen_View`, `Equipment_Store_View`\n- Validation: 5,375 actors saved; 2D obstacle-grid check verified routes to all ten rooms (script execution/connectivity only — not rendered/VR/perf validation)\n- Lighting: repaired unshadowed movable point lights (forward-render compatible). Preview lighting, can leak through partitions; needs a final lighting/perf pass\n\n## 2. Reference corridor (legacy)\n\n- Map: `/Game/NavalFireVR/ReferenceEnvironment/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Coursive`\n- 24 m corridor, ~2 m clear width, 2.7 m ceiling; control room, decorative props (2,054 actors in isolated validation)\n- Kept as the original reference; not part of menu routing\n\n## 3. Bow & sea scenery\n\n- Added to the expanded map by `Tools\\Python\\add_securex_bow_sea.py` (idempotent). Preserves interior and GameMode; original forward wall kept hidden with collision disabled\n- Forecastle: light-grey bulwarks, railings, braces, jackstaff, simplified static deck mount; small accessible viewing deck; `Bow_Sea_View` camera actor\n- Guardrails + hidden collision barriers confine desktop movement to the viewing deck (ocean and forecastle are NOT walkable; custom teleport must respect its own destination limits)\n\n## 4. Sea material (Experience_v2, 2026-11-02 update)\n\n- `/Game/NavalFireVR/Experience_v2/M_GentleSea`: slow, shallow moving ripples, analytical sky reflections; **non-colliding**, bounded away from the balcony\n- Material-driven surface animation — no Water plugin, fluid sim, transparency, buoyancy, or vertex waves. One opaque flat mesh + simple unlit sky sphere; ripples travel aft to suggest motion\n- Applied to the default map and all 41 scenario routes via the default world + shared fire-free environment\n\n**Known pitfall:** older builders passed rotation as positional args, which Unreal read as roll/pitch/yaw → door frames/bow rails protruded sideways. Fixed by explicit pitch/yaw/roll keywords in `build_securex_environment.py`; keep using explicit rotation keywords for any new geometry.\n\n## Related\n\n[[Fire Drill Scenario]] · [[Menu System]] · [[Python Scripts Index]]\n\n## 5. Ship-wide imported environment pass — applied 2026-11-07\n\nThe default expanded ship and shared `L_Ship_NoFire` environment now use imported steel/corrugated wall panels, detailed hatch leaves, room service pipes/lamp housings, wall kickplates and copied equipment surface materials. This supersedes the earlier corridor-only graphics result.\n\nEach world has 114 imported panels over 48 wall sections and service fittings in all ten rooms. Original collision and door openings remain; visible parked hatch leaves use imported meshes. Final surface textures use neutral tileable grain rather than pipe-atlas detail. The galley keeps its existing stainless interior surfaces with improved finishes. Existing equipment models mostly remain; detailed replacement engines/tools/appliances are not in this pack.\n\nSee [[Ship Realism — Imported Environment]] for the complete scope, actual counts, recovery maps, final screenshots and verification records. No Play/VR performance result is claimed.\n",
