      "excerpt": "Open work, ordered roughly by priority. Update statuses as items complete.",
      "body": "# TODO / Roadmap\n\nOpen work, ordered roughly by priority. Update statuses as items complete.\n\n## 🔥 High priority\n\n- [ ] **Classe F conversion** — the current kitchen fire is an *electrical appliance* fire temporarily behind the requested `Classe F` menu label. Convert to true cooking-oil behavior (per [[Curriculum & Sources]] agent guidance; scenario-specific agent selection).\n- [ ] **Role objectives** — develop role-specific objectives and interactions in the dedicated scenario maps (one fire playable from several roles via compact scenario data definitions).\n- [ ] **Objective event recording** — track alarm, doors/ventilation, power isolation, agent choice, reports, crew accountability, suppression, reignition, recovery → feeding debrief/timeline.\n\n## 🎯 Next milestone (per master reference)\n\n- [x] **2026-11-03 — In-level French objective guide (RDR2 style)** installed — see [[Objective Guide]]. v4 installer fixes the two failed-run defects (no duplicate GuideState graphs; HUD `target`→`self` wiring); **next step: editor restart → rerun → first Play validation**.\n- [ ] Briefing & learning objectives screen between menu and level\n- [ ] Debrief screen with event timeline + role-specific assessment\n- [ ] Extend beyond the kitchen drill: other fire classes when space/hazards/equipment/teaching logic exist\n- [ ] Key projected roles to flesh out first: DDL, DDI, groupe d'attaque (menu role list: groupe d'attaque, DDL, DDI, équipe d'alarme, équipe médicale, groupe soutien, groupe protection)\n\n## 📉 Performance\n\n- [ ] Profile Play in the current level (known stutter) and in a standalone build before setting a performance budget\n- [ ] Profile volumetric fire/smoke shaders before standalone VR use\n- [ ] Separate maps reduce loaded content but do **not** cure expensive shaders/effects — find the real hotspots\n\n## 🔬 Untested areas (test when possible)\n\n- [ ] Headset input: menu interaction (currently desktop-only) and drill VR bindings (requires XRFramework contexts active + VR pawn/GameMode)\n- [ ] Stereo appearance in-headset\n- [ ] Packaged build (SDK/toolchain required by Unreal packaging — settings already written to `Config`)\n- [ ] Headset frame rate on the expanded map\n\n## 🧹 Deferred / nice-to-have\n\n- [ ] Convert decorative firefighting-store props into real pickups/equipment (currently visual only)\n- [ ] VR teleport must self-restrict destinations (bow/ocean/forecastle not walkable)\n- [ ] Final lighting pass (preview lighting leaks through partitions; no shadows yet)\n\n## 📌 Standing user rulings (do not relitigate)\n\n- Menu design/typography/colors/sizes are final — never change them\n- All 42 menu routes exist; default route keeps the original expanded ship + existing fire\n- Signage style (light ivory Segoe UI Semibold on navy) must be preserved in future labels\n\n## Related\n\n[[Decision Log]] · [[Project Overview]] · [[Curriculum & Sources]]\n\n## Graphics follow-up — 2026-11-07\n\n- [x] Apply imported structural wall panels, hatch hardware and equipment surface finishes across all ten rooms and both ship environments — [[Ship Realism — Imported Environment]].\n- [x] Inspect corridor/room views, correct surface artifacts and panel-base gaps, and verify saved bindings, sign texts/positions and GameMode against backups.\n- [ ] Profile the upgraded maps in Play, standalone and the target headset; check stereo appearance and frame time.\n- [ ] Complete the final lighting pass and assess preview light leakage.\n- [ ] Obtain suitable detailed machinery, galley-appliance and firefighting-equipment models if full geometry replacements are wanted; current pack does not contain them.\n",
