      "updated": "2026-11-05",
      "excerpt": "The first playable slice: an electrical appliance fire on the galley rear prep counter, fought with a CO2 cylinder. Guide: Tools\\Docs\\RUNFIREDRILL.md.",
      "body": "# Fire Drill Scenario — kitchen CO2 drill\n\nThe **first playable slice**: an electrical appliance fire on the galley rear prep counter, fought with a CO2 cylinder. Guide: `Tools\\Docs\\RUN_FIRE_DRILL.md`.\n\n❗ This is **not** a cooking-oil fire (agent choice follows the [FIA guidance](https://www.fia.uk.com/static/uploaded/814f0141-6e91-4181-aaeb45ea82c55910.pdf)). Converting it to true **Classe F** behavior is the top pending item — see [[TODO — Roadmap]].\n\n## Install / repair scripts\n\n| Task | Command (Output Log > Cmd, Play stopped, map open) |\n|---|---|\n| Add drill | `py \".../Tools/Python/add_securex_fire_drill.py\"` |\n| Repair bottle controls | `py \".../Tools/Python/upgrade_securex_bottles.py\"` |\n\nHelpers kept beside the script: `securex_blueprints.py`, `securex_fire_logic.py`, `securex_vr_logic.py`, `securex_fire_audio.py`, `securex_bottle_logic.py`. Requires Unreal 5.8 Python Editor Script Plugin + Blueprint graph scripting APIs. Result runs as saved Blueprints/materials/sounds — no runtime Python. Successful rerun does **not** duplicate the drill.\n\n## The scenario\n\n- Fire on the galley rear prep counter; cylinder mounted in the hallway beside the galley hatch; power switch inside the entrance\n- **8 CO2 cylinders**, each with own charge + safety-pin state. Decorative scenery extinguishers converted to usable cylinders by the upgrade script\n- CO2: 15 s discharge, misses consume charge; effective suppression needs clear line-of-sight, ~0.35–2.6 m range, aiming at **each of 3 flame pockets**; remaining power allows re-ignition\n- **Completion** = all pockets out AND power isolated\n\n## Desktop controls\n\n| Key | Action |\n|---|---|\n| ZQSD + mouse | movement and free look; W/A movement replaced |\n| Hold Ctrl | crouch |\n| Hold Shift | sprint |\n| E | pick up nearest reachable bottle (within 1.8 m) |\n| P | remove safety pin |\n| Hold LMB | discharge (aim at flame bases, sweep) |\n| G | drop (with physics) |\n| F | isolate electrical supply (near galley switch) |\n| Backspace (←) | reset drill, refill and return cylinders; return player/camera to the start |\n\n## VR bindings (XRFramework)\n\nController finds `MotionControllerRightAim` on the player pawn and reads existing XRFramework input mappings without editing the pawn. Right grip: carry (hold near cylinder) · Right trigger: discharge · Left grip: pull pin while carrying · Left trigger: power isolator. Requires the project's input contexts active and the map's VR pawn/GameMode.\n\nPublic Blueprint API on the drill actor (for other pawns): `Grab(Grip)`, `Drop()`, `PullPin()`, `SetDischarge(Pressed)`, `IsolatePower()`, `RestartDrill()`.\n\n## Visuals & physics\n\n- Cylinder: red steel body, black CO2 label, brass valve, safety pin + ring, squeeze lever, hose, open horn; 12.5 kg\n- Effects: procedural volumetric flame/smoke materials, flickering light, cold discharge plume (stops at traced obstructions), generated positional audio loops\n- **Artistic approximation** — not fluid/combustion simulation; desktop carrying uses a fixed camera offset, not simulated arm weight\n\n## Validation history\n\nIsolated `.validation` project tested: pin interlock, charge use, misses, wall obstruction, suppression, re-ignition, depletion, drop, reset, duplicate prevention. Desktop keys (E/P/LMB/G/F/Home) were tested in the live editor before Home was replaced. The user confirmed Backspace works. The ZQSD/Ctrl/Shift installer compiled and saved its Blueprint and GameMode on 2026-11-05; live movement, crouch, and sprint still need checking. **Untested:** actual headset input, stereo appearance, packaged builds, headset frame rate. Volumetric shaders should be profiled before standalone VR.\n\n## Related\n\n[[Ship Environments]] · [[Curriculum & Sources]] · [[TODO — Roadmap]]\n",
