      "excerpt": "These updates are saved in the Unreal project. This note records them in the Obsidian vault as well. They persist when the project is reopened; editor Python commands are instal…",
      "body": "# Gameplay updates — 2026-11-05\n\nThese updates are saved in the **Unreal project**. This note records them in the Obsidian vault as well. They persist when the project is reopened; editor Python commands are installers, not required at runtime.\n\n## Current default route\n\nThe original menu design is preserved. Startup and game default map are `/Game/NavalFireVR/Menu_v1/L_NavalMenu`. Selecting **groupe d'attaque × Classe F** opens `/Game/NavalFireVR/ExpandedShip/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Expanded` with the current electrical-appliance CO2 drill. The menu label **Classe F** still awaits conversion to a cooking-oil scenario. The other 41 routes remain separate fire-free levels.\n\n## Saved gameplay changes\n\n| Feature | Current behavior | Saved asset / source |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Objective guide | French instruction at bottom center; larger white context and yellow action, dark shadow. Advances with the real drill state. | `/Game/NavalFireVR/Guide_v1/BP_NavalGuideHUD_vN` selected by the desktop GameMode; `Tools/Python/add_naval_guide.py`; [[Objective Guide]] |\n| Galley power sign | Physical sign reads **« Alimentation électrique »** on two lines. | Default expanded map; `Tools/Python/fix_naval_sign_and_restart.py`; [[Signage]] |\n| Reset | **Backspace (←)** resets the fire, CO2 cylinders, and state, then returns the player and camera to the starting location and standing height. | `/Game/NavalFireVR/FireDrill/Controls_001/BP_CO2_FireDrill`; [[Fire Drill Scenario]] |\n| Desktop movement | **ZQSD** replaces WASD; mouse looks around without a held button. | `/Game/NavalFireVR/Experience_v3/BP_NavalDesktopPawn_AZERTY`; [[Input & Controller]] |\n| Crouch and sprint | Hold **Ctrl** to lower the view/collision and slow down; hold **Shift** to sprint. | Same AZERTY pawn; `Tools/Python/install_naval_azerty_controls.py` |\n\nThe desktop GameMode `/Game/NavalFireVR/DesktopPreview/BP_SECUREX_DesktopGameMode` uses the saved AZERTY pawn and guide HUD. The menu uses its own GameMode and keeps its original appearance and behavior. VR controls have not been updated by these desktop changes.\n\n## Save and verification\n\nThe Unreal log shows the corrected sign/reset run reached `NAVAL_SIGN_AND_RESTART_OK` after saving and reloading the expanded map at 11:48 UTC. At 11:59 UTC it saved `BP_NavalDesktopPawn_AZERTY` and `BP_SECUREX_DesktopGameMode`, then logged `NAVAL_AZERTY_CONTROLS_OK`. The user confirmed Backspace works. Live ZQSD, crouch, and sprint behavior still needs checking in Play.\n\nFor future editor changes: **stop Play → File > Save All → close the editor**. The project reopens on the saved menu; choose the default route and **COMMENCER**. Saving preserves assets and settings, not a play session's current player position or fire progress.\n\n## Source guides\n\n- `Tools/Docs/RUN_NAVAL_GUIDE.md`\n- `Tools/Docs/RUN_NAVAL_SIGN_AND_RESTART.md`\n- `Tools/Docs/RUN_NAVAL_AZERTY_CONTROLS.md`\n- `Tools/Docs/NAVAL_SIMULATION_REFERENCE.md` — master project reference for future chats\n",
