      "body": "# Input & Controller\n\n*(2026-11-02 update; guide `Tools\\Docs\\RUN_EXPERIENCE_FIXES.md`; script `Tools\\Python\\polish_naval_experience.py`)*\n\n## Gameplay (desktop)\n\n- Gameplay **hides the cursor, focuses the game viewport, and captures mouse movement automatically** — look around by moving the mouse, no button held\n- `Shift+F1` releases the cursor during Unreal Play to reach editor controls\n- Implemented in `BP_NavalDesktopController`\n- Current pawn: `/Game/NavalFireVR/Experience_v3/BP_NavalDesktopPawn_AZERTY`, saved and selected by `BP_SECUREX_DesktopGameMode` on 2026-11-05. ZQSD replaces the engine's WASD movement; hold Ctrl to crouch, hold Shift to sprint. See [[2026-11-05 — Gameplay Updates]].\n- Backspace resets the drill and returns the pawn/camera to the starting position and standing height.\n\n## Menu controller (separate behavior)\n\n- `BP_NavalDesktopController` in the menu keeps a **visible pointer** and uses `CaptureDuringMouseDown`\n- Why: `NoCapture` prevents the engine game viewport from forwarding mouse-button presses; the menu also explicitly runs its mouse-position query when needed\n- Click rectangles scale with the rendered viewport\n\n## Verified in live Play (2026-11-02)\n\n- Left/right arrows for both selectors; clicking COMMENCER → entered `L_ddl_F` (DDL × Classe F)\n- Camera rotation from mouse movement **without** holding a button\n- Sea captures seconds apart confirm animated ripples; corrected galley doorway visually inspected\n- Drill keys E, P, LMB, G, F, Home were tested in-editor before Home was replaced with Backspace (see [[Fire Drill Scenario]])\n\n## Still untested\n\nHeadset input (VR menu pass not started), stereo appearance, packaged build performance. VR bindings for the drill require XRFramework input contexts — see [[Fire Drill Scenario]].\n\n## Related\n\n[[Menu System]] · [[Fire Drill Scenario]]\n",
