      "updated": "2026-11-05",
      "excerpt": "(Installed 2026-11-03; guide Tools\\Docs\\RUNNAVALGUIDE.md; builder Tools\\Python\\addnavalguide.py)",
      "body": "# Objective Guide\n\n*(Installed 2026-11-03; guide `Tools\\Docs\\RUN_NAVAL_GUIDE.md`; builder `Tools\\Python\\add_naval_guide.py`)*\n\n## What it is\n\nAn in-game instruction line in **French**, bottom-center of the screen, telling the trainee what to do next — requested in the exact style of a **Red Dead Redemption 2** objective screenshot:\n\n- enlarged Roboto text with **white context**, **yellow imperative/action**, and a soft **dark double-draw shadow**\n- no box, no icon, sentence case, persistent while valid\n- swaps text instantly as each step completes\n\n## Install (`Output Log > Cmd`, Play stopped)\n\n```text\npy \"C:/Users/user/Documents/Unreal Projects/NavalFireVR/Tools/Python/add_naval_guide.py\"\n```\n\n⚠️ Each run creates a new HUD revision `BP_NavalGuideHUD_vN`; the GameMode points at the newest. The script **never deletes** assets — script deletion of a half-built Blueprint crashed the editor (`ForceDeleteObjects` ensure). **After any failed run: restart the editor first (answer Don't Save), then rerun** — unsaved graph edits and broken pin links live only in memory. If the log flags a package as *potentially corrupt*, close the editor and delete that `Guide_v1` file in **Windows Explorer** (never a Python `delete_asset`). When the style is final, tidy old revisions manually in the Content Browser.\n\n- `GuideState()` on the drill is created **once**; later runs verify the census graph by name and repair only open pins (never `create_and_edit_function_graph` again — a second call builds a duplicate graph whose cross-graph links break compilation)\n- Creates a fresh HUD `BP_NavalGuideHUD` revision in `/Game/NavalFireVR/Guide_v1` each run\n- Sets `hud_class` on `BP_SECUREX_DesktopGameMode` (idempotent)\n- Prefers the playable `FireDrill/Controls_00N/BP_CO2_FireDrill` class, falling back to `Build_00N` when needed. The earlier `Build_001` lookup found zero actors in the live drill map.\n\n## Message set\n\n| Situation | Line |\n|---|---|\n| Spawn, far from galley | « Un incendie a éclaté en cuisine. Va le vérifier. » |\n| Near fire, no cylinder | « Prends le cylindre CO2 dans le couloir. (E) » |\n| Cylinder held, pin in | « Retire la goupille de sécurité. (P) » |\n| Pin out, power on | « Coupe l'alimentation électrique de la cuisine. (F) » |\n| Power isolated | « Extinction : vise la base de chaque foyer et balaie. (Clic gauche) » |\n| Spraying while powered | « Le courant alimente le feu : coupe-le d'abord. (F) » |\n| Trigger with no setup | « Saisis d'abord un cylindre CO2. » / « Retire d'abord la goupille de sécurité. » |\n| Charge nearly empty | « CO2 épuisé ! Appuie sur Retour arrière (←) pour recommencer. » |\n| Complete | « Exercice réussi ! Appuie sur Retour arrière (←) pour recommencer. » |\n\n## Behavior: strict sequence + smart warnings\n\nPer the user's chosen mode, the guide shows **one** instruction and only advances when that step is done; out-of-order attempts (trigger before pin/bottle, spraying while powered) override the line with a warning. It reads the drill's real variables — never fabricated state.\n\n## How it binds (design facts)\n\n- `BP_NavalGuideHUD` subclasses `AHUD`, draws on **`ReceiveDrawHUD`** every frame (same pattern as the menu HUD, untouched)\n- Finds the drill with `GetActorOfClass` (class path resolved at build time to the newest upgraded Controls_00N)\n- **v1 lesson (2026-11-03):** the graph plugin cannot read another Blueprint's member variables — `add_get_member_variable_node` only resolves the graph's own class (first run failed: `Failed to find member named Held`)\n- **v2 mechanism:** the drill gets one additive read-only function **`GuideState()`** with output pins `Held`, `PinRemoved`, `PowerIsolated`, `Complete`, `Trigger`, `Active`, `NearFire`, `TotalHeat`, `Charge`; the HUD calls it by full class path (proven call-node pattern) and reads the pins; `NearFire` = camera–`Fire0` distance < 10 m, computed inside the drill where the helpers already live\n- **v2.1 (same day):** the Return node's exec input is found with `find_execute_pin()` (the project's canonical lookup) instead of name probes; reruns complete an existing partial `GuideState` without re-declaring outputs — plugin probe logs ($ outputs via `add_graph_output_parameter`) confirmed which APIs exist\n- **v3 bugs found by two crashed runs (v4 fixes):** (1) reruns must **never** re-enter `create_and_edit_function_graph` for an existing function — the duplicate graph family makes `MakeLinkTo/BreakLinkTo` fire `different outer`/`not reciprocally linked` ensures and the compiler rejects *\"Return Node generates no code\"*; v4 verifies via `get_graph_editor()` on the graph found by a per-run census and repairs only open pins. (2) call nodes expose the Python-side `target=` as the node's `self` pin — the HUD's local re-implementation looked for a literal `target` pin and aborted with `Missing pin`; v4 calls through the helper's `g.call()`. `GetActorOfClass` output pin is `ReturnValue`.\n- A cascade of `SelectString` nodes picks the message; **completion has highest override priority**\n- Only on the drill map: the 41 fire-free routes and the menu draw nothing different\n- HUD revisions (v3+): each run makes a new `BP_NavalGuideHUD_vN`; no script deletes anything\n\n## Guidelines (recorded for all future scripts)\n\n- **Never call `delete_asset` on a Blueprint asset this plugin built, especially a partial one** —\n  `ForceDeleteObjects` can hard-crash (ensure) instead of raising. Use new revision names and let\n  the user tidy up in the Content Browser.\n- API quirks: cross-BP variable reads unsupported; function Return node exec found with\n  `find_execute_pin()`; `add_graph_output_parameter` exists and works; `GetActorOfClass` output\n  pin is `ReturnValue`; call-node `target` is the `self` pin — always route call wiring through\n  `Graph.call()` or `Graph.node()` instead of re-implementing it.\n- **Plugin API facts (UE 5.8 `BlueprintEditorLibrary`, from the engine headers):** node\n  enumeration is `list_all_nodes()` / `list_nodes_of_class(K2Node_FunctionResult)` — there is\n  no `list_nodes`; Return creation is `add_return_node()`; pin connection state is\n  `list_connected_pins()` — `is_connected`/`is_linked` never existed on `FBlueprintGraphPin`,\n  so older probes silently read \"disconnected\" and re-wired already-linked pins. All these\n  are `meta=(ScriptMethod)` statics, hence the node.method(...) call shape.\n- **Never call `create_and_edit_function_graph` (i.e. `Graph(bp, name)`) twice for the same\n  function** — it builds a duplicate graph; cross-graph pin links then trip `different outer`\n  ensures and the compiler dies on half-links. Detect via a graph census, open with\n  `get_graph_editor(found)`, and repair inside that single family only.\n\n## Validation status\n\nCurrent status (2026-11-05): the French guide is visible in the user's gameplay screenshots. Its action phrase is enlarged and yellow; Backspace replaces Home. The earlier v4 failure and recovery notes above are historical. The saved guide HUD, drill Blueprint, and desktop GameMode persist across editor sessions. See [[2026-11-05 — Gameplay Updates]].\n\n## Related\n\n[[Fire Drill Scenario]] · [[Menu System]] · [[TODO — Roadmap]]\n",
