      "body": "# Signage\n\n*(Installed 2026-11-02; guide `Tools\\Docs\\READABLE_SIGNAGE.md`; preview `Tools\\Docs\\SIGNAGE_PREVIEW.png`)*\n\n## The style (must be preserved)\n\n- Large **Segoe UI Semibold**, 64-point font atlas, **light ivory lettering on dark navy backing panels**\n- Upright, centered, size fitted to each fixture; equipment labels stay within physical fixtures\n- Yellow was only an example, not a requirement\n- ⚠️ The **menu keeps its original design/typography/colors/sizes — readability changes apply only to in-game panels, indications and identifying labels**\n\n## Coverage\n\n- Every TextRender label in the default ship map (**39**) and the shared fire-free environment (**21**) — reaches all 42 scenario routes, see [[Menu System]]\n- Door labels: upright, centered within enlarged navy plates; other fixed indications get dark backing matched to the lettering\n- The default drill map's galley isolation sign now reads **« Alimentation électrique »** across two lines. The first script run failed to save it; the corrected run saved and reloaded the map successfully on 2026-11-05. The shared fire-free map has no isolation sign. See [[2026-11-05 — Gameplay Updates]].\n\n## Assets & repair\n\n- Assets: `/Game/NavalFireVR/Signage_v1` (font assets, text material, panel material)\n- Repair script (Output Log > Cmd, Play stopped): `py \".../Tools/Python/improve_naval_signage.py\"` — marks corrected orientations; reruns reuse backing panels (no duplicates)\n- Sea, fire logic, role selections, and level routing are unaffected by the signage update\n\n## Related\n\n[[Ship Environments]] · [[Menu System]] · [[Python Scripts Index]]\n",
