      "excerpt": "(Implemented 2026-11-02 — verified in Unreal Play)",
      "body": "# Menu System\n\n*(Implemented 2026-11-02 — verified in Unreal Play)*\n\n## Maps and routes\n\n- Startup map AND game default map: `/Game/NavalFireVR/Menu_v1/L_NavalMenu` (set in `Config\\DefaultEngine.ini` + `DefaultGame.ini`)\n- **7 roles × 6 fire types = 42 distinct map routes.** Manifest: `Tools\\Docs\\MENU_ROUTES.json`\n- Default route: `groupe d'attaque` × `Classe F` → `/Game/NavalFireVR/ExpandedShip/Build_001/L_SECUREX_Expanded` (the current drill; the \"Classe F\" label is a user-requested menu default, and the electrical fire has **not** yet been converted to cooking-oil behavior)\n- Other 41 routes: independent persistent maps under `/Game/NavalFireVR/Scenarios/`, each loading the shared fire-free `/Game/NavalFireVR/Scenarios/L_Ship_NoFire` environment (same ship + sea, drill actors removed). Only the selected map + environment load at runtime\n- ⚠️ Edits to the shared `L_Ship_NoFire` environment affect **every** empty scenario\n- All 42 route targets exist and were verified\n\n## Menu design\n\n- Animated background: painting of the Moroccan FREMM 701 in the Firewatch menu-reference style, slow looping drift (saved HUD Blueprint). Art: `Tools\\Art\\Menu\\fremm_menu_v1.png` → imported texture `/Game/NavalFireVR/Menu_v1/T_FREMM_Menu`. Generation prompt record: `Tools\\Docs\\MENU_ART_PROMPT.md`\n- **The user declared the menu design \"already perfect\" — never change its typography, colors, or sizes.** Readability changes only apply to in-game panels/labels (see [[Signage]])\n- The menu map contains no ship geometry or fire simulation; all logic is saved Blueprints, no runtime Python\n- Desktop mouse/keyboard only so far — headset pointer/controller interaction needs a future VR menu pass\n\n## Controls\n\n- Click arrows beside **Role** / **Type de feu**; **COMMENCER** starts. Clicking the selected value also advances it\n- Keyboard: `R` cycle role · `T` cycle fire type · `Enter` start · `QUITTER` exits game/Play\n- Menu keeps a visible pointer and uses `CaptureDuringMouseDown` (`NoCapture` blocks the engine viewport from forwarding mouse-button presses); click rectangles scale with viewport\n- See [[Input & Controller]] for the mouse-look fix story\n\n## Builder\n\n- `Tools\\Python\\build_naval_menu.py` (+ `securex_blueprints.py` beside it) — **refuses to replace existing menu assets**. For another revision, use a new version folder and review map destinations first\n\n## Related\n\n[[Roles & Command Chain]] · [[Ship Environments]] · [[Input & Controller]]\n",
