      "body": "# Project Preferences\n\nUser rules mirrored from the project's `AGENTS.md`. These govern how work is done in NavalFireVR sessions.\n\n## File placement\n\n- Everything created for the project is placed **in the Unreal project folder**, not only in the chat workspace\n- Python editor scripts **and their imported Python helpers** go together in `Tools\\Python`\n- User guides go in `Tools\\Docs`, with runnable script paths pointing at the **project copies**\n- Every new/updated deliverable is **mirrored** into the Unreal project, and instructions must give **project paths**\n- Workspace copies kept when useful\n- Temporary validation outputs, caches, logs are **not** deliverables and need no mirroring\n\n## Process rules\n\n- **Read `Tools\\Docs\\NAVAL_SIMULATION_REFERENCE.md` at the start of every NavalFireVR session** (master reference: goal, role/fire menu direction, curriculum mapping, locations). `NAVAL_SAFETY_SOURCE.json` holds slide-indexed lecture text; original decks/photos in `Tools\\Docs\\NavalSafetySources`\n- Training logic must **cite deck + slide** from the four French lectures; consult original decks/photos for visual details text extraction misses\n- Update `NAVAL_SIMULATION_REFERENCE.md` as gameplay decisions are made\n- The Unreal project is the workspace root; normal write escalation covers it\n\n## Design rulings (from the user)\n\n- The main menu design was declared **perfect** — preserve its original typography, colors, sizes forever\n- Readability changes apply **only** to in-game panels, indications and identifying labels (not the menu)\n- Yellow was an example color, not a requirement; the installed signage style is **Segoe UI Semibold, light ivory on dark navy panels**\n- The menu default selection is **groupe d'attaque × Classe F** (label requested by the user; underlying fire behavior conversion still pending)\n- Scenario levels must be **separate levels**, not everything in one loaded ship map (existing Play session stutters)\n\n## Related\n\n[[Project Overview]] · [[TODO — Roadmap]]\n",
