      "updated": "2026-11-03",
      "excerpt": "Source: reference doc 2026-11-02. The default is groupe d'attaque.",
      "body": "# Roles & Command Chain\n\n## Installed menu roles (7)\n\nSource: reference doc 2026-11-02. The default is **groupe d'attaque**.\n\n1. Groupe d'attaque *(default)*\n2. DDL — overall damage control director\n3. DDI — intervention director\n4. Équipe d'alarme\n5. Équipe médicale\n6. Groupe soutien\n7. Groupe protection\n\nPaired with 6 fire types (A, B, C, D, **F (default)**, HC) → **42 distinct routes**, see [[Menu System]].\n\n## Organic command chain (lecture 1 slide 20; lecture 2 slides 6–12)\n\nCommandant · Second in command · Adjoint sécurité · Assistant sécurité · Maître sécurité · Service safety officers · Safety brigade.\n\n## Operational exercise roles (lecture 2)\n\n| Role | Core interaction | Slides |\n|---|---|---|\n| Discovering crew member / immediate intervention | Raise alarm, assess, attack only with suitable equipment, confine, report | 16–17 |\n| **DDL** (overall damage control director) | Maintain compartment plan & situation, issue directives, coordinate reinforcements | 19 |\n| **DDI** (intervention director) | Choose tactic, direct teams, report to DDL, track compartmentation | 20 |\n| Adjoint feu | Brief attack teams, talk to team leaders, manage reliefs | 22 |\n| Groupe d'attaque | Equip, receive orders, use thermal camera, attack, rotate teams | 23 |\n| Groupe de protection | Prepare hoses, protect boundaries, contain spread, manage extinguishing water | 24 |\n| Groupe de soutien | Isolate power & ventilation, verify confinement, manage access-route smoke | 25 |\n| Gestionnaire ARI | Track breathing-apparatus personnel & accountability | 26 |\n| Passerelle / poste de sécurité | Maintain plan, call/receive reinforcements, coordinate ship support | 27 |\n\n## Design idea\n\nA role changes the objectives and interactions **within** a scenario level; create a distinct level only when layout or active simulation differs materially (see [[Project Overview]] — design principles).\n\nOne fire should be playable from several roles via compact scenario data definitions. Objective events to record: alarm, doors/ventilation, power isolation, agent choice, reports, crew accountability, suppression, reignition, recovery.\n\n## Related\n\n[[Curriculum & Sources]] · [[Menu System]] · [[TODO — Roadmap]]\n",
