      "excerpt": "Applied scope: the default expanded ship and the shared fire-free ship used by the other scenario routes. The menu is separate.",
      "body": "# Whole-ship visual upgrade\n\nApplied scope: the default expanded ship and the shared fire-free ship used by the other scenario routes. The menu is separate.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Imported steel wall panels and corrugated bulkheads replace the visible cube walls within their original bounds, preserving original invisible collision and door openings.\n- Material copies add imported world-scaled roughness detail and subtle normal detail to existing machinery, stainless galley fittings, hoses, rubber, painted equipment, lockers, room surfaces and exterior fixtures. Original colours and existing detailed normals are retained. Signs, screens, glass and emissive materials are excluded.\n- Each of the ten rooms receives imported overhead service piping and ship lamp housings.\n- Ten detailed imported parked hatch leaves replace the visual procedural parked-leaf parts; original hatch frames remain. Two machine exhausts gain detailed imported pipe geometry.\n- Metal kickplates seal the bases of all 48 upgraded wall sections. Panel faces point toward corridor and room interiors.\n- Final equipment finishes use neutral tileable roughness grain and generic cloth, rubber or metal normals. UV-baked pipe atlas detail is not used on unrelated props.\n\nThe imported pack has no complete engine, firefighting suit, breathing apparatus, extinguisher or galley appliance models. Existing equipment geometry remains except for the imported pipe/hatch replacements. This pass is not a photoreal equipment model replacement.\n\n## Recovery and records\n\nBackups: `/Game/NavalFireVR/Realism_WholeShip_v2/Backups/L_BeforeWholeShip_0` and `L_BeforeWholeShip_1`.\n\nMaterial copies and backups live under `/Game/NavalFireVR/Realism_WholeShip_v2`. The original material assets are preserved. Original wall and parked-leaf parts remain in the map with their rendering hidden. Added decoration uses NoCollision.\n\n`SHIP_REALISM_WHOLE_SHIP_REPORT.json` records wall actors, new panels, per-component surface assignments and map saves. `SHIP_REALISM_HARDWARE.json` records detailed hatch replacements. `SHIP_REALISM_VERIFICATION.json` contains saved-asset readback checks including protected sign text/positions and GameMode comparison against backups.\n\n## Scripts\n\nProject scripts are in `C:\\Users\\user\\Documents\\Unreal Projects\\NavalFireVR\\Tools\\Python`:\n\n- `ship_realism_whole_ship.py`: main install, refuses duplicate installation.\n- `ship_realism_hardware.py`: final hatch and exhaust pass, refuses duplicate installation.\n- `ship_realism_verify.py`: reloads both maps and compares bindings, room coverage, wall collision and protected sign/GameMode state with backups.\n- `ship_realism_polish.py`, `ship_realism_panel_orientation.py`, `ship_realism_surface_noise.py`: applied finishing corrections. `ship_realism_finalize.py` runs panel orientation and verification.\n\nDo not rerun installers on an already upgraded map. Use the verification script for inspection. Recovery map names are fixed and preserved on retries.\n\nViewport inspection and property verification do not establish headset performance or gameplay behaviour. No Play/VR run is part of this visual pass.\n\n## Measured installation\n\nBoth ship worlds have 114 imported wall panels across 48 original wall sections, service runs and two lamp housings in each of ten compartments, ten imported parked hatch leaves, two detailed exhausts, and 48 wall kickplates. There are 26 copied equipment/environment materials. The initial main-map pass changed 5,982 material slots; the shared environment changed 5,478. These are component slot counts, not unique equipment models. Each world retains 1,690 old parked-leaf components with rendering hidden in favour of ten detailed imported leaves.\n\nSaved reload verification found no wall-collision or material-assignment failures; all 65 main-map and 21 shared-map sign texts/positions and the GameMode matched their recovery copies. See the verification JSON for the readback evidence. Preview PNGs are in `Tools/Docs/ShipRealismPreviews`.\n",
